---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
---

<PageLayout
    title="What Counts as Melbourne? – Suburble"
    description="How does Suburble define what suburbs are in Melbourne?"
>
    <h1 class="font-bold text-2xl">What Counts as Melbourne?</h1>
    <br />
    <p class="c0"><span class="c5"></span></p>
    <p class="c4">
        <span
            >Melbourne is a sprawling city. It completely engulfs more populated
            cities like
        </span>
        <span class="c1">
            <a class="c2" href="https://mapfight.xyz/map/melbourne/#london">
                London
            </a>
        </span><span>, </span>
        <span class="c1">
            <a class="c2" href="https://mapfight.xyz/map/melbourne/#bangkok">
                Bangkok
            </a>
        </span><span>, or </span>
        <span class="c1">
            <a class="c2" href="https://mapfight.xyz/map/melbourne/#istanbul">
                Istanbul
            </a>
        </span><span>
            &nbsp;when overlaid on top of eachother. And unlike cities like
            London, there is no clear boundary of where Melbourne ends and
            regional Victoria begins. For the purposes of Suburble, I have
            arbitrarily defined a suburb as being part of Melbourne proper it
        </span>
        <span class="font-bold"> is within 5km of an suburban train line.</span>
        <span>
            "Suburban" in this context is every electric train, as well as the
            train line to <a
                class="link"
                href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Rail_Plan"
                >Wyndham Vale and Melton</a
            >, as they function like suburban train lines (even if they are run
            by V-Line).
        </span>
    </p>
    <br />
    <p>
        <span class="c5">
            Some areas that are considered part of &ldquo;Greater
            Melbourne&rdquo; like the Mornington Peninsula are not included as
            part of this game. This decision is less of a statement about
            Melbourne and more about game design, as guesses in Suburble are
            based in part on train lines.
        </span>
    </p>

    <br />

    <p>
        <span class="c5">
            If you'd like to read more about Suburble, check out the <a
                class="link"
                href="/about">About page,</a
            > or you can read through the <a
                class="link"
                href="https://github.com/avavuvu/suburble">source code</a
            > on my GitHub.
        </span>
    </p>
</PageLayout>
